<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ponce, Puerto Rico</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ponce is the largest city on the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-ponce-de-leon">Juan Ponce de León</a> y Loayza, great-grandson of the island's first governor. It grew rich from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and trade in the 19th century. On 21 March 1937 police fired on a Nationalist Party march there, killing 19 people in the Ponce massacre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ponce-puerto-rico.jpg" alt="Ponce, Puerto Rico" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Mtmelendez · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castillo_Serralles.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
